Article 6 (Limitation of Liability)

Even if the Licensor is found liable for damages, the total aggregate liability of the Licensor to the user shall not exceed the total amount of fees actually paid by the user to the Licensor during the six (6) months preceding the event giving rise to such liability.

In no event shall the Licensor be liable for lost profits, loss of business opportunity, loss or corruption of data, or any indirect, consequential, special, or incidental damages.

Article 7 (Term and Termination)

This Agreement becomes effective on the date the user first uses the Software and remains in effect as long as the user continues to use the Software.

If the user breaches this Agreement, the Licensor may immediately terminate this Agreement and suspend the user's use of the Software without prior notice.

Upon termination of this Agreement, the user shall immediately cease using the Software and delete all copies of the Software in its possession or control.

